# Cloudflare Pages redirects — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# 301s for handbook lessons whose URL slugs were renamed or split — the v1.14
# chapter split (2026-08-17) and the v2.8.0-v2.12.0 teaching redesign
# (2026-09-02). Old bookmarks and search entries land on the successor lesson
# instead of a 404. Mapping source: the redesign spec
# (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-handbook-teaching-redesign.md).
#
# EXACT PATHS ONLY. Placeholder/splat rules here once looped forever with
# Cloudflare's directory normalization (301 -> internal slash normalization ->
# rule matches again) — never add pattern rules to this file. Both the
# trailing-slash and the bare form are listed because Cloudflare only
# normalizes the slash on paths that resolve to a real asset — dead paths
# never hit that normalization, so the bare form needs its own rule.
#
# Demo-layer file: only the demo serves /landing/docs routes, so fork
# initialization removes it together with the landing pages (LANDING_PATHS in
# scripts/apply-template.ts + the "Remove project landing page" step in
# .github/workflows/setup.yml). Rule shape, live targets and channel sync are
# pinned by tests/redirects.test.ts.

